i think this is an example of a perfect or close to room, the main things to note are:
1)at 13s in livesplit you want to stall a bit to bait the crystal hunter into shooting;
2)at 15s in livesplit you want to react to if they're shooting or not, and if they are i think you want to walljump and then dash into the above platform, i did a normal jump bc i kind of improvised, but i think its too hard to do consistently in runs;
3)at 17s in livesplit its better to do wj just simply to avoid landnt;
4)the ending strat for the early control, it requires an overbind bind to right stick down, slash as soon as you see the crystal hunter enter the screen and make sure your first pogo hits the ddark crystal, then copy what i did;
here i got extremely good rng which is why the room is so fast but i could consistently get a 32 room if the crystal hunter gave good rng and mid 33 if the they gave bad rng, for reference current comsob i think has a 33.98 the only problem for this strat is that the crystal hunter climb is extremely hard to not get hit on so its very risky
2 extra things to add that i didnt do in the video but i found out later on are better:
1)at 16s in livesplit you can do snake wjs to avoid both landnt, i think its harder but worth cause if you get landnt youre fucked pretty much;
2)at 11s in livesplit you can snake wj on the platform, its hard and needs to be done at the top of the platform, but it makes the hunter climb a easier and more consistent;

ok i cooked cursed jump and heres the result on how long of a frame window you can do the wings based on how short of a repress you do:
0f repress: 10f;
1f repress: 9f;
2f repress: 6f;
3f repress: 4f;
>4f repress: impossible;
this is all assuming you didnt get an airwalk after the cdash*
as a refence for the cue, the last possible frame of the wings input is the same for all of them and is exactly 3-4f after the apex of the jump depending on how you define the apex, i define it as the last frame where the speed is positive so 4f, the frame window to wj after depends both on the repress and when you pressed wings so i cant think of a rule to figure it out(not that it really matters too much), generally you want to avoid the extremes of the frame windows and you want to avoid 2-3f represses cause those made it really hard to get the wj in TAS(i had to change where i turned around to make sure i didnt lose too much height cause of out tight it got), i think that if you get a 3f repress its pretty much impossible to get the wj with any amount of consistency, and with a 2f you probably only have a 1-2f** window where its reasonable, tho these are just guesses cause i didnt lab too much the insides of the frame windows

translating all of this into something useful inputs-wise, you want to press wings at the apex of your jump but later is better than early, tho you dont wanna be too far off on either direction, and you want a near perfect repress otherwise its very hard to get the wj afterwards, from experience doing a ninsta as the wj didnt significantly impact the difficulty of the trick

reminder that a 0 frame repress is when there are no physics frames where the game register no press, but you still unpressed during a graphics frame so it will register a repress, its basically the faster repress possible in the game and for humans its effectively impossible to get it 100% of the time because we cant see when a physics frame starts
